From: Project Luma <engineering@projectluma.org>
Date: Mon, 8 Sep 2026 01:20:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] compositor: Fix opaque region after surface-content backport

The background-effect backport moves MetaSurfaceActor's shaped texture behind
MetaSurfaceContent, but Fedora 50.4 retains one opaque-region accessor outside
the upstream commit's original context. Resolve the texture through the public
actor helper like the other adapted call sites.

This is a narrow Fedora 50.4 compatibility fix; it adds no behavior beyond the
upstream background-effect series.
---
 src/compositor/meta-surface-actor.c | 5 +----
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/compositor/meta-surface-actor.c b/src/compositor/meta-surface-actor.c
--- a/src/compositor/meta-surface-actor.c
+++ b/src/compositor/meta-surface-actor.c
@@ -855,9 +855,6 @@ MtkRegion *
 meta_surface_actor_get_opaque_region (MetaSurfaceActor *self)
 {
-  MetaSurfaceActorPrivate *priv =
-    meta_surface_actor_get_instance_private (self);
-
-  return meta_shaped_texture_get_opaque_region (priv->texture);
+  return meta_shaped_texture_get_opaque_region (meta_surface_actor_get_texture (self));
 }
 
 void
-- 
2.55.0
